 VERDICT
  - World level. H: -8% [-13,-4], a real but small step (interval excludes zero, inside the tolerance). Raw join: -77% [-78,-76], steps as it must, so the test has power. MODIS control: -6% [-11,-2], a real but small step (interval excludes zero, inside the tolerance). H with the control divided out: -2% [-3,-1] (burned area cancels in this figure; it is not independent evidence).
  - Level by region (14). H FAILS in 3: TENA -13% [-22,-3]; BOAS -29% [-43,-13]; CEAS -24% [-34,-13]. Real but small step in 2: NHAF, SHAF. The MODIS control FAILS in 4: BOAS -19% [-32,-4]; CEAS -21% [-32,-10]; SEAS +15% [+1,+33]; AUST -13% [-25,-1]. H fails while the control holds (points at the record): TENA. Control fails while H does not (H's pass is no evidence there): SEAS, AUST. H departs from the control by more than the tolerance: BOAS -13% [-17,-9].
  - Level by country (25). H FAILS in 8: Russian Federation -28% [-42,-12]; Central African Republic -13% [-18,-8]; South Sudan -10% [-14,-6]; Myanmar +25% [+7,+47]; Madagascar -22% [-30,-13]; China -44% [-56,-31]; Argentina +22% [+1,+45]; Cameroon -16% [-23,-9]. Real but small step in 6: Democratic Republic of the Congo, Angola, Zambia, Tanzania, Nigeria, Ethiopia. The MODIS control FAILS in 11: Democratic Republic of the Congo -11% [-17,-6]; Russian Federation -17% [-29,-3]; Australia -13% [-25,-1]; Central African Republic -13% [-17,-8]; South Sudan -11% [-15,-7]; Myanmar +36% [+16,+59]; Indonesia +20% [+2,+49]; Madagascar -21% [-29,-13]; China -45% [-57,-30]; Argentina +27% [+6,+51]; Cameroon -13% [-19,-6]. H fails while the control holds (points at the record): none. Control fails while H does not (H's pass is no evidence there): Democratic Republic of the Congo, Australia, Indonesia. H departs from the control by more than the tolerance: Russian Federation -14% [-19,-9]; Canada -12% [-23,-0].
  - Level by class (3). H FAILS in 0: none. Real but small step in 2: middle third, large fires (most km2/hotspot). The MODIS control FAILS in 0: none. H fails while the control holds (points at the record): none. Control fails while H does not (H's pass is no evidence there): none. H departs from the control by more than the tolerance: none.
  - Variability pooled over the 14 regions: r = 0.88 for H in the estimated years and 0.79 in the VIIRS years (MODIS: 0.88 and 0.81). The estimated years do not follow burned area worse than the VIIRS years. Before 2012 H is a function of MODIS and both products are seeded with MODIS hotspots, so a high r there is partly built in.
  - Variability by region and country (annual totals against burned area, r). Lower before 2012 than after by more than 0.2: United States (H 0.67 vs 0.94; MODIS 0.73 vs 0.97); China (H -0.26 vs 0.89; MODIS -0.36 vs 0.85). H worse than its own MODIS input before 2012 by more than 0.1 (real VIIRS doing the same after 2012 makes this expected): none.
  - Seasonality by region and country (mean monthly cycle against burned area, r). Lower before 2012 than after by more than 0.1: China (H 0.44 vs 0.77; MODIS 0.34 vs 0.77). H worse than its own MODIS input before 2012 by more than 0.1 (real VIIRS doing the same after 2012 makes this expected): none.

